1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gustaf Eneskjöld, † 1719-01-00 in Russian captivity in Moscow. Freerider at the Turku and Pori County Cavalry Regiment 1674. Corporal at the Turku and Pori County Cavalry Regiment 1675-02-00. Adjutant 1675-07-12. C
2 CONC ornet 23-12-1675. Lieutenant 1676-11-00. Captain lieutenant 1678-03-27. Horsemaster 27-11-1678. Confirmation power of attorney 14-10-1679. Major 11-11-1700. Colonel and head of the regiment 1701-08-07. He witnessed the battle of N
2 CONC arva, was captured at Errastfer 1701-12-30, exchanged in 1708, again captured at Poltava 1709-06-28. Married 1680-07-11 in Nikolai parish, Stockholm (Wn.) to baroness Hilgard Elisabet Rehbinder born 11-10-1663, † 11-12-1735. Daugh
2 CONC ter of the colonel and baron Bernhard Rehbinder and his 1st wife Elisabet Munck af Fulkila. Children: Helena Elisabeth. Married 1:o 1713 to commander Samuel Chytreen, † 1720-09-11 at Herrala in Lempäälä. Married 2nd 1721-06-15 at 
2 CONC Herrala to the rust holder Matias Tammelin born 1690, † 1764-11-12 in his 1st marriage. Bernt Johan Eneskjöld born at Lyttskär and baptized 11/11/1683 baptized there, † 1726. See Tab. 7 ex. TAB 3 Carl Magnus Eneskjöld born 14-11-1
2 CONC 688? and baptized 1689-01-14 at Lyttskär. Entered service in 1700. Corporal at the Turku and Bjornborg county cavalry regiment. Second Cornet at the Turku and Pori County Cavalry Regiment 1707-02-22. Second lieutenant 1709-04-05. 
2 CONC Captured 1709-09-01 at Perevolotjna. † unmarried 1721-07-00 in Totma during Russian captivity. Gustaf Fredrik Eneskjöld born 1685 at Lyttskär, † 1686-02-28. Elisabet Dorotea Eneskjöld born at Lyttskär and baptized there 1686-04-29
2 CONC , probably † 1694-05-05 at Lyttskär. Gustaf Eneskjöld born 1687 at Lyttskär, † 1764. See Tab. 8 ex. TAB 4 Charlotta Eneskjöld born at Lyttskär and baptized there 15-11-1692, † 08-05-1740 at Lyttskär. She received support from the 
2 CONC refugee commission in 1716. Married to the master of horse at the Turku county cavalry regiment Johan Ludvig Taube, † around 1716 in Russian captivity. Anna Christina Eneskjöld born on Lyttskär and baptized there 1691-07-28, † 176
2 CONC 0-06-14, Married to schoutbynachten Evert Johan Taube baptized 1681, † 1759. Otto Reinhold Eneskjöld born 1694-06-29 on Lyttskär, died unmarried in the battle at Storkyro 1714-02-19. Field sergeant at the Bjornborg county infantry
2 CONC  regiment. Ensign at Björneborg county's infantry regiment 1712-03-02. Henrik Johan Eneskjöld born 1697, † 1743. See Tab. 9 Anna Hildgard Eneskjöld born 1699-09-19 in Lyttskär, † 1768-03-21 in Vallby, Hagby parish, Uppsala county 
2 CONC and buried 1768-04-02 in Husby-Lyhundra church, Stockholm county. Married to her brother-in-law's cousin, Major Jakob Rudolf Taube, in his 2nd marriage, born 1688, † 1766.
2 CONT Lähde: https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Eneskj%C3%B6ld_nr_585
2 CONT Captured in Errastfer 1701-12-30
2 CONT
2 CONT Released in the exchange of prisoners in 1708, imprisoned again in Pultava on 1709-06-28
2 CONT
2 CONT The owner of the Lyttylä manor: "Already in 1655, Engelbrekt Eneskiöld had received a mortgage in the engagement court on a 3 1/2 eyry-sized part of Lyttylä, which he had bought from the heirs of the former owner, Maalina Antintyt
2 CONC äre in Ruohoniemi and Matti Antinpoja in Hyve-
2 CONT here. After Engelbrekt Eneskiöld l) died, Lyttylä had to be his
2 CONT to his son Kustaa Eneskiöld's. On August 12, 1682,
2 CONT with the help of the king with a letter, he had his ownership rights confirmed.
2 CONT Soon after this, however, the reduction was extended to the little ones
2 CONT tilus and Lyttylä were ordered to cancel the year 1682
2 CONT with tax. However, the space was immediately given back to ''Kustaa Eneskiöldin''
2 CONT to cultivate for life. Kustaa Eneskiöld died in 1715 and
2 CONT after him, Lyttylä was ruled successively by Eneskiöld-
2 CONT related persons: Captain Berndt J u h a n a Eneskiöld 2) († 1726),
2 CONT major Berndt Juhana Eneskiöld 3) († 1777) and lieutenant Berndt
2 CONT Kustaa Eneskiöld 4) († 1829)." Source: Satakunta, kotisetutuikkija I, published by Satakuntalainen osakunta, in Helsinki 1907, OSAKEYHTIÖ KAUPPAKRIJAPAINO. 173. https://julkaisut.satakuntalainenosakunta.fi/satakuntasarja/pdf/Satak
2 CONC untasarja_I.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fi.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yyterin_kartano
2 CONT
