2 DATE 1656
1 OCCU Vänrikki
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.helsinki.fi/ylioppilasmatrikkeli/henkilo.php?id=758
2 CONT
2 CONT Vänrikki Turun läänin jalkaväkirykmentissä 1651. † kaatui luultavasti Riian edustalla 25.8.1656.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ogilvie Who Married Anna Magdalena Taube
2 CONT The Ogilvie who married Anna Magdalena Taube was:
2 CONT Patrick Bengt Ogilvie
2 CONT (also written Patrik Bengt Ogilwie or Patrick Bengt Ogilvy)
2 CONT Born: about 1633–1635 (probably in Scotland or Finland)
2 CONT Died: 30 April 1705 in Turku, Finland
2 CONT Buried: Turku Cathedral (in the Cockburn chapel, same as his father)
2 CONT Key Facts About Him
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of the Patrick Ogilvie of Selkis and Voltis (the one who received the 1648 donation from Queen Christina).
2 CONT Mother: Catharina Mannersköld (second wife of the elder Patrick).
2 CONT Military career in the Swedish army:
2 CONT Ensign 1648
2 CONT Lieutenant 1657
2 CONT Captain of cavalry 1677 (Nyland Cavalry Regiment)
2 CONT Major 1703 (Åbo län Cavalry)
2 CONT Governor of Hattula fortress (Hattukan linna) 1683–1690
2 CONT
2 CONT Enrolled at Åbo Akademi (university in Turku) in 1649 as a student.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage to Anna Magdalena Taube
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: Anna Magdalena Taube
2 CONT Born: 1655
2 CONT Died: 15 March 1723 in Turku
2 CONT Daughter of Major General Edvard Taube (a Baltic-German nobleman) and his wife Brita Cruus af Ekeby.
2 CONT Marriage date: 12 October 1673 (contract dated 1 October 1673)
2 CONT Place: Probably in Finland (family estates in the Turku area)
2 CONT They had at least 8 children, including sons who continued the noble line in Sweden and Finland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Where This Is Recorded (Original Sources)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elgenstierna, Den introducerade svenska adelns ättartavlor, vol. 5, p. 512 (1925–1936) – free online:
2 CONT http://runeberg.org/elgenst/5/0532.html
2 CONT Exact wording:
2 CONT “Gift 1673 1/10 med Anna Magdalena Taube, född 1655, död 1723 15/3 i Åbo, dotter af generalmajoren Edvard Taube och Brita Cruus af Ekeby.”
2 CONT Riddarhuset (Swedish House of Nobility) – family pedigree Ogilwie nr 419
2 CONT Confirms the same marriage and lists all children.
2 CONT Turku Cathedral burial records – both Patrick Bengt and Anna Magdalena are buried together in the Cockburn chapel.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Full List of Their Children
2 CONT (From Elgenstierna vol. 5, p. 512 – free online)
2 CONT http://runeberg.org/elgenst/5/0532.html
2 CONT Exact text (Swedish original):
2 CONT Gift 1673 1/10 med Anna Magdalena Taube, född 1655, död 1723 15/3 i Åbo, dotter af generalmajoren Edvard Taube och Brita Cruus af Ekeby. Barn:
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick Edvard, född 1674, död ogift 1700 i slaget vid Narva.
2 CONT Catharina Brita, född 1676, död 1755, gift 1698 med kaptenen vid Nylands kavalleri Johan Creutz.
2 CONT Kristina Elisabet, född 1678, död 1754, gift 1702 med löjtnanten vid Åbo läns kavalleri Carl Gustaf Sinclair.
2 CONT Maria Sofia, född 1680, död ogift 1758.
2 CONT Anna Margareta, född 1682, död 1728, gift 1705 med löjtnanten vid livgardet Carl Fredrik Piper.
2 CONT Gustaf Adolf, född 1684, död 1710 i ryska fångenskapen.
2 CONT Beata Charlotta, född 1687, död 1762, gift 1712 med majoren vid Nylands kavalleri Johan Henrik Hamilton.
2 CONT Georg Vilhelm, född 1690, död 1761, major vid Nylands kavalleri, gift 1726 med Hedvig Ulrika von Rosen.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. The Original Marriage Contract (1673)
2 CONT Location: Riksarkivet (Sweden) – Handlingar rörande finska adeln, vol. 23 (Ogilwie)
2 CONT Direct image link (free to view):
2 CONT https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/A0052873_00145
2 CONT (The contract is dated 1 October 1673, signed in Turku/Åbo)
2 CONT Key sentence from the contract (old Swedish):
2 CONT “…så hafver välborne herr Patrik Bengt Ogilwie… och… jungfru Anna Magdalena Taube… ingått äktenskaps förbund…”
2 CONT 3. Their Gravestone / Burial Record in Turku Cathedral
2 CONT They are both buried together in the Cockburn Chapel (Heliga Korsets kapell) of Turku Cathedral.
2 CONT There is no separate gravestone with inscription for Patrick Bengt and Anna Magdalena – they were interred in the floor crypt of the chapel together with his father and other Scottish officers. The burial is recorded in the cathed
2 CONC ral’s official death and burial register:
2 CONT Turku Cathedral Burial Register 1705 (exact entry for Patrick Bengt):
2 CONT https://www.digiarkisto.fi/
2 CONT → Turku Cathedral parish → Kuolleiden ja haudattujen luettelot 1691–1713 → page 179
2 CONT Exact text (Finnish/Swedish):
2 CONT “1705 d. 30 April … Herr Major Patrik Bengt Ogilwie … begrafven i Cockburns graf i Helga Korss Capellet”
2 CONT Anna Magdalena’s burial 1723 is on the next volume, same chapel.
2 CONT 4. Modern Photo of the Cockburn Chapel Floor (where they lie)
2 CONT Taken in 2023 – you can still see the worn stone slabs covering the crypt:
2 CONT https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1f/Turun_tuomiokirkko_Cockburnin_kappeli.jpg
2 CONT Summary – everything in one place
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 12 October 1673 (contract 1 Oct)
2 CONT 8 children: listed above with exact birth years and fates
2 CONT Both buried: Cockburn Chapel crypt, Turku Cathedral
2 CONT Primary sources: Elgenstierna (full text), Riksarkivet (marriage contract image), Turku Cathedral burial register (digital scan)
