1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Karin (Katarina) Hansdotter''' (1539 - 1596), was the royal mistress of King John III of Sweden in the 1550s before his marriage during his time as Prince and Duke of Finland.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''(Although it has''' been claimed that  Karin is believed to be the daughter of Hans Klasson Kökkemäster, there is no actual documents or evidence that he was  father of Karin).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Karin worked as''' a servant in the court of Queen Katarina Stenbock when John met her sometime in the middle of the 1550's, (before 1556) and she followed him to his fief in Finland where she was installed as his mistress.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1561, before''' John's marriage to Catherine Jagellonica of Poland, Karin was married to Klas Andersson Westgöte (d. 1563), a friend and servant of John, and given the Wääksy Manor in Kangasala in Finland. When John became K
2 CONC ing in 1568, he continued to support Karin and his illegitimate children.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1572 Karin''' was married again, her earlier husband was murdered by Erik XIV in 1563, to a Lars Henrikson Hordeel (d. 1591). In 1576, Lars was nobled by John on the condition that he took care of his issue with Karin. In 15
2 CONC 77, she became the neighbour of the deposed queen Karin Månsdotter. Karin died in 1596 during the great Finnish peasant rebellion and did not have to witness the plundering of her estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Källa: Lars Ericson - Johan III och Lars-Olof Larsson - Arvet efter Gustav Vasa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruotsin Kunigas Juhana III  rakastajatar  Tieto Genilehti Suomen Sukututkimus Seura
