1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Baron''' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustav_Evertsson_Horn '''Gustaf Evertsson Horn of Marienburg'''] was a Finnish-Swedish military and politician. He was a member of the Privy Council of Sweden and Governor
2 CONC  General.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Horn, the son of''' Field Marshal [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evert_Horn '''Evert Horn af Kanckas'''], was born in 1614 in Southwest Finland, at the time a part Sweden. He became captain in 1635, and a colonel in 1640. In 16
2 CONC 51, he was, along with cousin Henrik Horn, raised to a baron. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gustav Horn became''' a member of the Swedish Privy Council in 1653, and in the following year, he was assigned the role of Governor General of Ingria and Kexholm, an office he left for the assignment of Governor General of Fin
2 CONC land in 1657. In 1656 he was appointed general, in 1658 rikstygmästare and in 1663 field marshal. The latter year he also became Governor General of Bremen-Verden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gustav Evertsson Horn''' died in Stade, Germany, in 1666.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He had with his''' wife baronesse Barbro Kurck (d.1658) another daughter Brita Horn (1647-1651).
