2 CONC s ättlingar var, enligt en berättelse, frälsebonder som var i rusttjänst. De kan inte identifieras från bevarade dokument.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''NOTE! Ragnar Rosén has in ''Vehkalahden pitäjän historia'' claimed that Olof Mattsson Horn's father was Mathis von der Sahe, which he assumes to have come to Vehkalahti in 1350's, - according to a story saved in year 1618. The 
2 CONC story has been preserved in two other editions in addition to that used by Rosén. These editions indicate that Sahe didn't came to Vehkalahti, but to Kalax village in Porvoo parish and that he came under King Eric of Pomerania. He
2 CONC  can not be an ancestor of the Horn family. Sahe's descendants, according to a story, were ''frälse'' farmers who were in equestrian service. They can not be identified from the surviving documents.'''
