1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arvid_Kurck '''Arvid Kurck'''] (also known as ''Arvid Kurki''; 1464 in Vesilahti – 22 July 1522 in Öregrund) was the Roman Catholic Bishop of Turku from 1510 to 1522. He was a member 
2 CONC of the Finnish noble family Kurki of Laukko. Kurck is considered to be the last truly Catholic bishop of Finland since his successors started to hesitantly promote the Reformation.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Arvid Kurck studied''' at the University of Paris in 1480s. He was a supporter of Sten Sture the Younger who was against the re-establishment of Kalmar Union. 1520 Kurck survived the Stockholm Bloodbath as he did not visit the 
2 CONC coronation of Christian II. Two years later Kurck took part on the uprising against King Christian. As the rebellions were defeated, Kurck fled to Sweden and was drowned in a shipwreck near the town of Öregrund.
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT <br/>
