1 NAME Richard /Clerck/
2 GIVN Richard
2 _MARNM Clerck
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 12 DEC 1604
2 PLAC Happingworth
2 ADDR
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 BURI
2 DATE 1668
2 PLAC Klara kyrka
2 ADDR
3 CITY Stockholm
3 STAE Uppland
3 CTRY Sweden
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 APR 1668
2 ADDR
3 CITY Stockholm
3 CTRY Sweden
1 OCCU Vice amiral, Amiral
1 TITL Adm.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Richard Klerck den yngre, adlad Clerck=
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Adelsvapen===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Clerck_nr_442 '''Richard Klerck''' den yngre, adlad '''Clerck'''], född 1604-12-12 i Happingworth, Skottland (''not on a map''). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Skeppskapten vid''' svenska amiralitetet 1628. Holmkapten 1630. Holmmajor 1638. Major i 3. eskadern av [https://www.geni.com/people/Claes-Fleming/6000000000064412280 Claes Flemings] flotta 1644 och i [https://www.geni.com/peopl
2 CONC e/Erik-Ryning-till-Sund/6000000009262408239 Erik Rynings] flotta 1645. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Adlad 1648-12-07''' (introducerad 1649 under n:o 442). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Amirallöjtnant 1654'''. Holmamiral 1655. Vice amiral i [https://www.geni.com/people/Klaus-Bielkenstierna/6000000008507394270 Claes Bielkenstiernas] flotta 1657. Befälhavare för flottan i Wismar 1657. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Död 1668-04-06''' i Stockholm, jordfäst i Jakobs kyrka och begraven 1668-12-03 i Klara kyrka, där hans vapen före branden sågs [Zf]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1:o''' 1633-01-13 med '''Lunetta Macklier''', född 1616-03-21. Död 1634-07-13, dotter av handelsmannen Jakob Macklier i Stockholm och Lunetta Raverding. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 2:o''' 1640-05-17 i Nikolai församling, Stockholm (Wn) med '''Maria Welshusen'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift ? 3:o''' Med '''Brita Lindorm''', dotter av vice amiralen Hans Hansson samt syster till majoren Henrik Hansson, adlad [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Lindorm_nr_439 Lindorm].) Rickard Klerck, adlad Clerck, var icke s
2 CONC on till Johan (Hans) Clerck [KA. Kammarkoll. Reg. K. brevet 1647 20/11].
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Riksarkivet===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/Sbl/Mobil/Artikel/14886 '''Richard Clerk''' (den yngre), före adlandet ''(?)'' '''Clerck'''], f. 12 dec. 1604 i Happingworth i Skottland, d 6 apr. 1668 i Stockholm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Fadern var antagligen''' holmamiralen Johan Clerck. Skeppskapten vid svenska amiralitetet 1628; holmkapten 1630; holmmajor 1638; ledde en handelsexpedition med några kronans skepp till Amsterdam 1640; major i tredje eskadern av
2 CONC  Klas Flemings flotta 1644 och i Erik Rynings flotta 1645; adlad 7 dec. 1648; bevistade riksdagarna 1649, 1650, 1652, 1654, 1655 och 1664; förordnad att verkställa generalmönstring i Västergötland 12 maj 1652; överförde engelske a
2 CONC mbassadören B. Whitelocke till Lybeck med skeppet Amarant 1654; amirallöjtnant 1654; holmamiral 20 jan. 1655; vice amiral i Klas Bielkenstiernås flotta 1657; befälhavare för flottan i Wismar nov. 1657.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1)''' 13 jan. 1633 med '''Lunette Macklier''', f. 21 aug. 1616, d 13 juli 1634, dotter till handelsmannen Jakob Macklier i Stockholm.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 2)''' 17 maj 1640 i Stockholm med Maria Welshussen; 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift (?) 3)''' med Brita Lindorm, dotter till vice amiralen Hans Hansson.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''C: s första''' självständiga befäl var ledningen av en fraktexpedition till Amsterdam med fyra skepp samt bojorten Svarta Hund, samtliga lastade med stockholmsborgares köpmansvaror (1640). I Kalmar måste bojorten utbytas mot sk
2 CONC eppet Tigern, emedan den under vägen förlorat sin stormast. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Under 1643-45''' års danska krig förde C. befäl på Klas Flemings flotta (1644) och Erik Rynings flotta (1645) och deltog bl. a. i slaget på Kolberger hejde (1 juli 1644). Efter att ha utnämnts till holmamiral - en befattning, s
2 CONC om ungefär motsvarar varvschef i våra dagar - deltog han som vice amiral i danska kriget 1657 och övertog efter amiral Klas Bielkenstiernas avsegling på hösten befälet över den i Wismar kvarlämnade flottan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Denna låg''' tämligen overksam hela nov.; den 4 dec. erhöll C. av konung Karl Gustav order att hemsegla, och den 21 dec. kom han till Dalarö. Här överraskades flottan av vintern och blev liggande ända till följande vår, då fart
2 CONC ygen gingo upp till Stockholm. Under de tider, då C. icke var till sjöss, skötte han såsom holmamiral de löpande ärendena vid huvudstationen i amiral Bielkenstiernas frånvaro.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''C. erhöll''' (20 nov. 1647) i förläning ett hemman Krisslinge i Danmarks socken i Uppland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===University of St. Andrew's===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=4138&id2=4138 '''Richard Clerk'''] was born in Happingworth, Scotland in 1604 and was either the son of Captain William Clerk ([https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.
2 CONC php?id=4349 SSNE 4349]) or the son of John/Hans Clerk the elder ([https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=4159 SSNE 4159]), who was also a Swedish holm admiral. Although as Hans was the brother of Richard Clerk the e
2 CONC lder ([https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=4137 SSNE 4137]) this would have made Richard Clerk the younger his nephew. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1628 Clerk''' became a ship's captain in the Swedish admiralty. That year he was sent to Norrland, Finland, and Aland to bring "lodjor" to Stockholm. Clerck was soon appointed to Danzig. However, in August 1629 Chancellor Ax
2 CONC el Oxenstierna ordered him to take over command of the ships at Pillau on the death of vice-admiral Hans Horn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1630 he was''' 'holm captain' and the yard captain at Skeppsholm shipyard. He was promoted to holm major in 1638 (although one source notes it as 1641). In 1640 he was sent to Amsterdam with 5 vessels on a mercantile mission
2 CONC  (just when the Covenanters were seeking military supplies from the Swedes). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''By 1644 he was''' major in the 3rd squadron of Claes Flemming's fleet, and served as adjutant to the commander on the Dalarö-based fleet. He was the chief on Svardet and partook in the sea battle on 1 July. The military college
2 CONC  instructed him and Benjamin Bonnell to deliver 10 lasts of coal to the artillery smithy in 1647. Clerk thereafter served in Erik Ryning's fleet in 1645. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was ennobled''' in 1648, 7th of December, and introduced into the Swedish House of Nobility in 1649 under n:o 442. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Clerck acted as''' muster-master general in 1652 for Västergötland. The following year his ship Stockholm (co-owned with Benjamin Bonnel) was taken by English Privateers leading to  protracted court hearings in England. In 1654
2 CONC  Clerk was promoted to lieutenant admiral, and by 1655 he was 'holm admiral' although his duties at Skeppsholmen (Stockholm shipyard) re. shipbuilding and ship furnishing remained unchanged. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Two years later''' he became vice-admiral in Claes Bielkenstierna's fleet, and the same year, 1657, he commanded the fleet in Wismar. During 1658-1660 Clerck retained sole responsibility for Skeppsholmen. In 1633 he married Lun
2 CONC etta Maclean ([https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=5434 SSNE 5434]), daughter of the Scottish merchant James Macklier ([https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=5433 SSNE 5433)] of Stockholm, althoug
2 CONC h she died in June the following year. He was married two further times, on both occassions to Swedes one of whom was called Brita Lindrom. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Clerk had a sister''', Elizabeth ([https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=2836 SSNE 2836]), who married twice to Scottish officers, first James (Jakob) Drummond ([https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.ph
2 CONC p?id=1622 SSNE 1622]), then Jacob Sinclair ([https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=3441 SSNE 3441]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Clerck died on 6 April''' 1668 in Stockholm and was apparently succeeded by his "brother" (?) lieutenant admiral Hans Clerck .
2 CONT
2 CONT * A. Zettersten, Svenska Flottans historia aren 1635-1680, (Norrtelje, 1903), p.598; Biografiska Anteckningar om Officerare vid Orlogsflottan 1600-1699, p.111; A letter can be found in 'Krigskollegium Kancelliet; Adressatregistrat
2 CONC ur till Krigskollegiets Registratur 1631-1654', on "öppen sedel till honom och Benjamin Bonell att undsätta pa någon tid artillerismedjan 10 laster stenkol 28/8/1647"; For the ship Stockholm see TNA HCA 13/65 ff.62-65 The Claim of
2 CONC  Benjamin Bonnell and Richard Clerck (plus depositions), 20 August 1651; Svenska Adelns Ättartavlor, vol. 2, p.23, p.142; A. Zettersten, Svenska Flottans Historia Åren 1522-1634 (Stockholm, 1890), p.258; Uppsala University Library
2 CONC , Palmskiöldiska Samlingen 422, Lunetta Macklier - Here Clerck is noted as Rotgert Klerck, E. Wendt, Amiralitetskollegiets historia part 1 1634-1695, (Stockholm, 1950), p.91, 94, 97, 103, 140, 153, 156, 194, 213; Rikskansleren Axe
2 CONC l Oxenstiernas skrifter och brefvexling, first series IV, pp. 586-8.
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT <br/>
