1 NAME Margaret Scott de Balwearie
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 1520 AND 1545
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biographical Summary from Wikitree:
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Margaret (also recorded as Janet) was born about 1530 daughter to Scott of Balwearie in Fife. However the Scott family also for long held lands in the Carse of Gowrie at Flawcraig and had many associations with their neighbours Ki
2 CONC nnaird of that Ilk and Ogilvy of Inchmartine. The Birth Brief of Patrick Ogilvy attested at Perth in 1646 gives his great-grandmother as daughter to Scott of Balwearie but does not indicate which of the lairds was her father. He w
2 CONC ould have been Sir Willaim Scott either IXth or more probably his son of that name the Xth laird.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1550 Margaret Scott married John Langland portioner of Cullace and Little Buttergask in Perthshire
2 CONT
2 CONT John Langlands and Margaret Scott had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick b. 1550c mar Helen Hay
2 CONT Elizabeth mar William Ogilvy of Balgay
2 CONT
2 CONT By a decree of the Lords of Council at the instance of Margaret Scott and John Langlands her spouse on 28 Mar 1569/70 an Obligation was made by George Haliburton of Pitcur, as cautioner surety for Thomas Haliburton in Buttergask, 
2 CONC that Thomas would cease from all further occupation of the town and lands of Buttergask. This was witnessed at Pitcur on 8th April 1569 by George and David Haliburton.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 14 Jan 1594/95 John granted his son Patrick a quarter of the lands of Collace and a quarter of the lands of Little Buttergask where he lived. The liferent of these lands were reserved to John and his wife Janet (sic) Scott. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ National Records of Scotland CS7/43 see [1]
2 CONT ↑ RMS Vol vi 203 see [2]
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ RMS Vol vi 203 see [1]
2 CONT ↑ National Records of Scotland CS7/43 see [2]
2 CONT ↑ RMS Vol vi 203 see [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Information provided by Patrick Ogilvy (1606-1674) for his nobilization in Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT ..."Patricii Ogiluie Vice - Collonelli praedicti Nativitatis Legitimae et Ingenuitatis Testimonium fidele daremus, Praesertim cum omnibus pene Nostratibus constaret Patricium Ogiluie Vice-Colonellum praedictum legitime natum, bapt
2 CONC izatum et educatum, Nec non ex generosis et ingenuis parentibus Sancto Matrimonii Vinculo coram veneranda Ecclesia junctis legittime procreatum fuisse, Patre nimirum qvondam Willielmo Ogiluie de Balgaÿ ex domu de Inchmartine et ''
2 CONC Matre quondam Elizabetha LangLands filia domini de Collace intra Vice-Comitatum praescriptum, Ac etiam ex parte Patris Auia Monorgund de eodem, Proavia Haÿ de Meginch,''         '''et Mater sui Aui Rosse de Cragie''',       ''Et s
2 CONC imiliter ex parte Matris Auia Scot de Balwerie,   Mater suae Auiae Aito ne de eodem, Ac Mater sui Aui Wishert de Logie.'' Propterea Nobilissimus et Potentissimus Comes Joannes Comes de Perth Dominus Drummound et Stobhall, Nec non 
2 CONC Nobilissimus et Potentissimus Comes Joannes Comes de Kingorne, Dominus Lyon et Glames, Nec non Nobillissimus et Potentissimus Comes Jacobus Comes de "Finlatore" Dominus Deffurd, Nec non Nobilissimus Dominus Patricius dominus de De
2 CONC ffurd: Nec non Honorabiles et Potentes domini Dominus Patricius Ogilui de Inchmartine Dominus Thomas Blaire de Balthyoke, Virigraues et generosi Coram Nobis pro dicto tribunali praesentes Juramento adacti et axaminati, de more ela
2 CONC tis Brachüs expansis manibus et in coelum erectis digitis":.... 
2 CONT Translation:
2 CONT "His mother was formerly Elizabetha Langlands, daughter of Lord de Collace within the prescribed Vice-County, and also on his father's side Grandmother Monorgund of the same, Great-grandmother Haÿ of Meginch, and Mother of his Gra
2 CONC ndfather Rosse of Cragie, and similarly on his Mother's side Grandmother Scot de Balwerie Mother of his Grandmother Aito of the same, and the mother of his Grandfather, Wishert of Logie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generally about Scotts of Balwearie:
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/scotts_of_balwearie/page/23/mode/1up?view=theater
