1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JOHN LANGLANDS OF COLLACE AND LITTLE BUTTERGASK ==
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikitree:
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Langlands-183
2 CONT
2 CONT "Biography
2 CONT John was born about 1530, son to David Langlands and Agnes Wishart. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1550 he married Margaret Scott daughter to the laird of Balwearie in Fife..
2 CONT
2 CONT John Langlands and Margaret had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick b. 1550c mar (1) daug of Ross of Craigie (2) Helen Hay
2 CONT By a decree of the Lords of Council at the instance of Margaret Scott and John Langlands her spouse on 28 Mar 1569/70 an Obligation was made by George Haliburton of Pitcur, as cautioner surety for Thomas Haliburton in Buttergask, 
2 CONC that Thomas would cease from all further occupation of the town and lands of Buttergask. This was witnessed at Pitcur on 8th April 1569 by George and David Haliburton.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 14 Jan 1594/95 John granted his son Patrick a quarter of the lands of Collace and a quarter of the lands of Little Buttergask where he lived. The liferent of these lands were reserved to John and his wife Janet (sic) Scott. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ RMS Vol vi 203 see [1]
2 CONT ↑ National Records of Scotland CS7/43 see [2]
2 CONT ↑ RMS Vol vi 203 see [3]
2 CONT [edit"
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1573: Charter by which Tom Tullie of Kynmonth confirms that he has given certain parts of the lands of Kunmonth to Issobelle Langlands. The land was to be held by in conjunct fee and liferent by Issobelle and her husba
2 CONC nd David Tullie, son and apparent heir of Tom Tullie of Kynmomth, and afterwards by their lawful male heirs, whom failing by the nearest heir whatsoever of David Tullie. The charter follows from a contract of marriage dated 26 Feb
2 CONC ruary 1572, between David Tullie and Issobelle Langlands, her father, David Langlands, portioner of Culless, and his son John Langlands. Tom Tllie of Kynmonth reserved his own liferent. This charter was confirmed under the Great S
2 CONC eal of Scotland on 2 January 1578-79. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/775/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 2824]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 January 1586: Charter by which John Langlands of Little Buttergask confirms that he has sold (vendidit) his one quarter part of the lands of Collace, and one eighth part of the lands Brydingstoun, in the sheriffdoms of Fife 
2 CONC and Forfar. to Helen Hay, daughter of Peter Hay of Leys. His charter follows from a contract of marriage between his son and apparent heir, Patrick Langlands, and Helen Hay and her father, Patrick Hay of Leys. The land is to be he
2 CONC ld by Helen and her lawful male heirs by Patrick Langlands, whom failing by Patrick's nearest male heir whatsoever bearing the name and arms of Langlands. The land in question was occupied by Davind Langlands, father of John Langl
2 CONC ands of Little Buttergask, and his liferent interest was preserved by this charter. The charter of John Langlands of Little Buttergask was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 6 December 1591. [https://archive.org/details
2 CONC /registrummagnisi05scot/page/669/mode/1up RMS 1580-93: charter number 1973]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1546-1580. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, MA., Advocate. (H. M. G
2 CONC eneral Register House, Edinburgh, 1886), 1180 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1580-1593. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, MA., Advocate. (H. M. G
2 CONC eneral Register House, Edinburgh, 1888), 1155 pp. including indices and errata]’’’
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Langlands-183 Biographical Summary from Wikitree] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ohn was born about 1530, son to David Langlands and Agnes Wishart. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1550 he married Margaret Scott daughter to the laird of Balwearie in Fife..
2 CONT
2 CONT John Langlands and Margaret had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick b. 1550c mar (1) daug of Ross of Craigie (2) Helen Hay
2 CONT By a decree of the Lords of Council at the instance of Margaret Scott and John Langlands her spouse on 28 Mar 1569/70 an Obligation was made by George Haliburton of Pitcur, as cautioner surety for Thomas Haliburton in Buttergask, 
2 CONC that Thomas would cease from all further occupation of the town and lands of Buttergask. This was witnessed at Pitcur on 8th April 1569 by George and David Haliburton.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 14 Jan 1594/95 John granted his son Patrick a quarter of the lands of Collace and a quarter of the lands of Little Buttergask where he lived. The liferent of these lands were reserved to John and his wife Janet (sic) Scott. [3]
2 CONT
