1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT == ANDREW OGILVIE (aka ANDERS OGILWIE or OGILUIE) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[Swedish] Anders Ogilwie, från grefskapet Perth. Gift  med Bessetha Monargund of Monargund,  dotter af James Monargund och Joneta  Edmundsdotter Hay.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[English Translation by Google] Anders Ogilwie, of the county of Perth. Married to Besseta Monargund of Monargund, daughter of James Monargund and Joneta Edmundsdotter Hay.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Ogilvy-of-Inchmartine/6000000023473109244?through=6000000009523462686
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Information provided by Patrick Ogilvy (1606-1674) for his nobilization in Sweden ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''"Patricii Ogiluie Vice - Collonelli praedicti Nativitatis Legitimae et Ingenuitatis Testimonium fidele daremus, Praesertim cum omnibus pene (eller "sene"?) Nostratibus constaret Patricium Ogiluie Vice-Colonellum praedicutm legi
2 CONC time natum, baptizatum et educatum, Nec non ex generosis et ingenuis parentibus Sancto Matrimonii Vinculo coram veneranda Ecclesia junctis legittime procreatum fuisse, Patre nimirum qvondam Willielmo Ogiluie de Balgaÿ ex domu de I
2 CONC nchmartine et Matre quondam Elizabetha LangLands filia domini de Collace intra Vice-Comitatum praescriptum, Ac etiam ex parte Patris Auia Monorgund de eodem, Proavia Haÿ de Meginch, et Mater sui Avi Rosse de Cragie, Et similiter e
2 CONC x parte Matris Auia Scot de Balwerie Mater suae Auiae Aito ne de eodem, Ac Mater sui Aui Wishert de Logie. Propterea Nobilissimus et Potentissimus Comes Joannes Comes de Perth Dominus Drummound et Stobhall, Nec non Nobilissimus et
2 CONC  Potentissimus Comes Joannes Comes de Kingorne, Dominus Lyon et Glames, Nec non Nobillissimus et Potentissimus Comes Jacobus Comes de "Finlatore" Dominus Deffurd, Nec non Nobilissimus Dominus Patricius dominus de Deffurd: Nec non 
2 CONC Honorabiles et Potentes domini Dominus Patricius Ogilui de Inchmartine Dominus Thomas Blaire de Balthyoke, Virigraues et generosi Coram Nobis pro dicto tribunali praesentes Juramento adacti et axaminati, de more elatis Brachüs exp
2 CONC ansis manibus et in coelum erectis digitis":...."'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Translation by Google ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Ogiluie Vice - Collonelli Let us give a faithful testimony of the aforesaid Nativity and Ingenuity. that he had been legitimately born before the venerable Church had been joined, namely that the father was once William
2 CONC  Ogiluie of Balga from the house of Inchmartine and the mother of the late Elizabeth LangLands daughter of lord de Collace within the direction of the Vice-County The mother of her grandfather Rosse de Cragie, and similarly on the
2 CONC  part of her mother's grandmother Scot de Balwerie, the mother of her grandmother said not of the same, and the mother of her grandfather Wishert de Logie. Therefore the Most Noble and Most Powerful Count John Earl of Perth Lord D
2 CONC rummound and Stobhall Lord of Deffurd: And not the Honorable and Powerful Lord Patrick Ogilui of Inchmartine The Lord Thomas Blaire of Balthyoke, Virgraues and Gentlemen, present before Us before the said tribunal.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Unatributed Biography of Sir Patrick Ogilvie of Inchmartine ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ..."VI. Sir PATRICK OGILVIE of Inchmar∣tin, who succeeded him,Ibidem. and got a charter from king James V. of the lands of Balgillo, and many others, anno 1538.He got also a charter from queen Mary, terrarum dominicalium de Drimmy
2 CONC ,Ibidem.&c. anno 1548.He married,Stewart's hist. of the royal family, page 170. 1st, Marian Stewart, daughter of Thomas lord Innermeath, by whom he had a son, William, his heir apparent. He married, 2dly, Janet, daughter of Pa∣tri
2 CONC ck, fourth lord Gray,Chart. in pub. archiv. ad ann. 1541. by whom he had two daughters.1. Margaret, married to Patrick Hay of Megginch,Ibidem. ancestor of the earl of Kinnoul.2. Janet, married to John Kinnaird of that ilk.VII. WIL
2 CONC LIAM, only son and apparent heir of sir Patrick of Inchmartin, married E∣lizabeth, daughter of Patrick Kinnaird of Inch∣ture, ancestor of lord Kinnaird, and died be∣fore his father,Lives of the offic. of state.anno 1558, leaving i
2 CONC ssue, by the said Elizabeth Kinnaird, a son, VIII. Sir PATRICK, who succeeded his grandfather, and got a charter, under the great seal, domino Patricio Ogilvie, &c.Chart. in pub. archiv. of the lands and barony of Inchmartin, and 
2 CONC others, anno 1593.He married Margaret, daughter of sir George Haliburton of Pitcur, Lives of the offic. of state by whom he had two sons.1. Sir Patrick, his heir.2. William, who having been witness to the slaughter of Patrick Kinn
2 CONC aird of Inchture, got a remission under the great seal, Willielmo Ogilvie, filio legitimo Patricii Ogilvie de Inch∣martin, &c.Chart. in pub. archiv. dated 8th December 1594.He was succeeded by his eldest son, IX. Sir PATRICK, who,
2 CONC  in his father's lifetime, got a charter from king James VI. Patricio, juniori de Inchmartin,Ibidem.et Annae Camp∣bell suae sponsae, baroniae de Inchmartin, &c. dat∣ed 8th January 1611."...
2 CONT
