2 CONT https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=6103 Alexander Wilhelm Ramsay was born in 1680 in Jackarby. In 1696 he volunteered for the Nylands och Tavastehus Cavalry where he became an NCO in November 1699. He eventually
2 CONC  rose in rank to become a lieutenant colonel in the Åbo and Björneborgs län cavalry where he served until April 1722. Ramsay died in March 1761. He married Margareta Catharina Nöding in 1704 and Anna Sophia Wright in 1755.
2 CONT
2 CONT A. Lewenhaupt, Karl XII:s Officerare Biografiska anteckningar (2 vols., Stockholm, 1920), II, p.530.
