1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Lars Siggesson d.ä=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Sigge Sparre af Rossvik and Margareta Bengtsdotter Färla
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sparre_af_Rossvik_nr_7#TAB_2 '''Lars Siggesson the Elder, to Simonstorp'''] in Grolanda parish, Skaraborg county and to Bysta in Asker parish, Örebro county, which his 2nd wife inherited in 14
2 CONC 52.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Squires. Was''' district governor in Frökind district in 1464. Councillor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1473 in the autumn in Vadstena.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Married 1st in the 1430s''' to Märta Mårtensdotter, daughter of Mårten Svan and Ragnhild Håkansdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Married 2nd 1442'''-01-21 at Simonstorp to '''Ingeborg Bengtsdotter''' in her 2nd marriage (married 1st to the squire Bengt Tomasson, who carried a Sparre in his 2nd marriage), living widow in 1486, daughter of Bengt Larsson (r
2 CONC ödbjälke) and Margit Clausdotter Dowt.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sparre_af_Rossvik_nr_7 Noble family Sparre af Rossvik no. 7, by Adelsvapen Geneologies]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TABLE 2'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lars Siggesson the elder, (son of Sigge Larsson,''' Tab. 1), to Simonstorp in Grolanda parish Skaraborgs län and to Bysta in Askers parish Örebro län, which his 2nd wife inherited in 1452 3 . Squire. Was district chief in Fröki
2 CONC nd's district in 1464 1 . National Council. Died in 1473 in the autumn in Vadstena. '''Married in the 1430s to Märta Mårtensdotter 7 , daughter of Mårten Svan and Ragnhild Håkansdotter. Married 2nd 1442-01-21 at Simonstorp 3 to In
2 CONC geborg Bengtsdotter in her 2nd marriage (married 1st to the armsman Bengt Tomasson, who carried a Sparre in his weapon, in his 2nd marriage), lived widowed in 1486, daughter of Bengt Larsson (red beam) and Margit Clausdotter Dowt.
2 CONC '''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Peder Larsson .''' Squire. to Stola in Strö parish Skaraborg county, which he obtained with his 1st wife. Called Peder Bonde 4 , gunsmith. Lived in 1481, but was dead in 1490 7 . Married 1st to Ingegerd Tordsdotter , died 
2 CONC before 1485, daughter of Tord Pyting to Stola and Hemfred NN Married 2nd 7 to Ragnhild Turesdotter , who lived as a widow in 1493, daughter of the knight and lawman in Västergötland Ture Jönsson ( Black Skåning ) and Birgitta Henr
2 CONC ik's daughter Snakenborg .
2 CONT * 2. ''Sigge Larsson ,'' the younger. National Council. Died 1509. to Bysta in Askers parish Örebro county and Skofteby in Härene parish Skaraborg county, which he obtained with his first wife, and Ågården in Råda parish Skaraborg
2 CONC  county, which he in 1492 built into a manor house. Born 1442. Armsman. Riksråd 1477–1496 6 . Participated in the succession election in 1499, but not as councilor 6 . However, then witnessed a council meeting in 1505 6 . Died 150
2 CONC 9 between 6 and 10 May. 'He bore in his arms a red Sparre in a golden field, and on his helmet a crown of gold with five red flags on either side.' Married 1:o 1470 or just before to Brita Bengtsdotter , to Skofteby, died 1485 and
2 CONC  buried in Skara cathedral, daughter of the district chief and gunsmith Bengt Andersson (Öra) and Ragnhild Göstafsdotter. Married 2nd 1486-09-06 (morning donation letter) Göksholm to Kerstin Månsdotter , who lived as a widow in 15
2 CONC 19, daughter of the lawman, knight and councilor Måns Bengtsson ( Night and Day ), and his 3rd wife Ermegård Fikkesdotter Bülow.
2 CONT * 2. A daughter. Married to Bengt N. N. ​
2 CONT * 2. Bengta , died childless. Married. On 1507-03-31, the Riksrådet passed judgment between her nephew Peder Bengtsson and Lienne's niece's husband Lindorm Brunsson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Skofteby&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=5&postid=sdhk_39417&tab=post#tab 39417]
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 14700000, Skofteby(?)
2 CONT Content: The Knight Svarte Åke Jönsson, lawman in Södermanland, announces that he has returned to '''Laurens Siggesson''' a farm in Saleby (in Slöta parish, Vartofta district), which farm he had taken from [https://www.geni.com/pe
2 CONC ople/Karl-Bengtsson-F%C3%A4rla-till-Nyby/6000000027877347569Karl Bengtsson] during the time Åke Jönsson was chieftain at Axvall (1462-264). Karl Bengtsson's wife's father had disputed with '''Laurens Siggesson''' about the farm bu
2 CONC t the latter had rightfully bought it (14511018, B 16 fol. 66v-67r).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Skofteby&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=7&postid=sdhk_29697&tab=post#tab 29697]
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 14740100 Content: The squire Sigge Larsson in Skofteby renews and confirms the exchange his father''' Lars Siggesson''' made with Bishop Hans in Skara, whereby the bishop received Ulläraff (now Ullered in Otterstad parish,
2 CONC  Kålland district) with...
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Skofteby&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=6&postid=sdhk_29348&tab=post#tab 29348]
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 14720000, Skofteby Content: The respondent Åke Jönsson announces that he has returned to Lars Siggesson the farm Saleby (in Slöta parish in Västergötland), which he had taken from [https://www.geni.com/people/Karl-Bengtsso
2 CONC n-F%C3%A4rla-till-Nyby/6000000027877347569 Karl Bengtsson (Färla)] while he (the issuer) was chieftain at Axvall. There had been a dispute between Lars Siggesson and Karl Bengtsson's wife's father about this farm
2 CONT
