1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Måns Nilsson to Ahtis==
2 CONT
2 CONT Måns Nilsson to Ahtis in Lemu parish, to Haapaniemi in Pirkkala, which latter estate he had to cede to the crown in 1557 due to debt.
2 CONT District judge in Lower Satakunta in 1533. Bailiff in Kokemäki County from 1535 to 1545.
2 CONT
2 CONT Received a royal letter in 1537 to take back property from Turku Cathedral, to which he had proof of ownership, and in 1540 the right to possess Pyhäjoki farm in Mynämäki parish, which he had acquired from his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Appointed in 1540, together with Jöns Vestgöte, to command all soldiers in Finland. In 1542, he was given Stockholm Castle and the city in trust and in an honest castle lease. In 1545, after Nils Grabbe, he was appointed as comman
2 CONC der of Viborg, he requested to be dismissed that year due to ‘weakness and hernia,’ but was told to remain there over the winter. In 1550, he received a fiefdom in the forest region of Mynämäki until further notice. He was dismiss
2 CONC ed in 1555, after King Gustav's visit to Viborg, accused of ‘disloyalty, rudeness and ignorance’; he is believed to have died around 1560. Unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://runeberg.org/frfinl/0009.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Måns Nilssons exchange of Manna in Lemu for Mårthen Nilssons part of Pyhäjoki (Helgå) i Mynämäki (Virmo). Suomen asutuksen yleisluettelo -arkisto - Lemu, jakso 21; Kansallisarkisto: https://astia.narc.fi/uusiastia/viewer/?fileId=5
