2 NICK de Johnstoun
1 NAME Lt. Col. Edward Johnstone
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 ADDR
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 ADR2 Pernaja Church
3 CITY Pernaja
3 CTRY Finland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 OCT 1649
2 ADDR
3 CITY Riga
3 STAE Livonia
3 CTRY Latvia
1 OCCU Lieutenant Colonel
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://runeberg.org/frfinl/0222.html
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=2734
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Johnstone started his service as non-commissioned officer in 1623 in captain William Johnstone's [SSNE 570] company (William was very probably a relative). Edward then became an ensign with the Nyland regiment in 1624. In 1
2 CONC 630 he became a captain for a company of infantry and by 1635 he was the regimental quartermaster. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His first wife was Elin Salomonsdotter, whom he married in 1630 and through whom he gained land near Porvoo, Finland. However he divorced her in 1642 due to her illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1638 he gained promotion to major. In 1639/1640 he was lieutenant colonel of a Nyland regiment. At some point here he married his second wife, Katherine Guthrie [SSNE 6264], daughter of major Robert Guthrie [SSNE 4679], and wid
2 CONC ow of lieutenant colonel John Lichton [SSNE 4360]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1645 he commanded his own distinct regiment with the rank of lieutenant colonel. Despite a letter from the authorities stating he would be granted the next vacant colonelcy of a Finnish regiment in 1647, he appears to have died
2 CONC  before he could take on his own command.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He received inheritance rights to land in Finland: firstly through his first marriage (Seitlaks) and secondly through donation (Tervik). He died on 15 October 1649 in Riga, after appointing his relative, Colonel Francis Johnstone 
2 CONC [SSNE 2736], as his son's guardian. His wife Katherine died in 1650.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Swedish Riksarkiv, P. Sondén, Militära chefer i svenska arméen och deras skrivelser; Swedish Krigsarkiv, Muster Roll, 1624/5; 1625/4; 1626/4; 1630/21; 1631/9-11; 1632/8,9; 1635/1; 1636/12; 1638/3,16,19,24-27; 1639/13-15; 1640/10; 
2 CONC 1641/13; 1642/11; 1643/13; 1644/13,15; 1645/18; 1646/11; 1647/11,14; 1648/13; 1649/8 DEAD 6.8.49; Several letters can be found in 'Krigskollegium Kancelliet; Adressatregistratur till Krigskollegiets Registratur 1631-1654' dated be
2 CONC tween 15/3/1638 to 29/5/1647; J. Ramsay, Frälsesläkter i Finland intill stora ofreden (Helsingfors, 1909), p.209.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Some correspondence pertaining to his affairs post-mortem can be found in: Riksarkivets ämnessamlingar. Personhistoria https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/A0069764_00151#?c=&m=&s=&cv=150&xywh=2304%2C2516%2C3409%2C1966 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clan_Johnstone
