1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://runeberg.org/frfinl/0223.html '''Edvard Johnstone''']. Löjtnant, lefde 1669 i Reval.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''† före 1672 1/8''' då hans halfsyster, Elisabet Lichton, vid häradsting begärde att bli fri för hans efterlämnade gäld 
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT So, Acording to Jully Ramsay,  Edward had a step-sister the name of whom was '''Elisabet Lichton'''. The verbatim translation is half-sister. That implies the Elisabet was John Lichton's daughter. But that does not quite add up. 
2 CONT
2 CONT What am I missing?
2 CONT
2 CONT If she came to ask be free of Edward's ''gäld''. His debt? Didn’t he inherit Tervik? 
2 CONT
2 CONT Step sister might suffice given that it does not imply being related by blood. In that case, John (or ''Johan'') had a daughter not listed - but... 
2 CONT
2 CONT All logic dictates (father and mother) that Ed Jr. was born in Porvoo. He was last spotted in Tallinn, but did he die there? 
2 CONT
2 CONT The reference to Elisabet (probably Elizabeth) seems legit enough, but... Step-sister and half-sister are not synonymous to me.
