1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Dj%C3%A4kn,_Lydikas%C3%B6nernas_%C3%A4tt#TAB_6 '''Bengta Lydekadotter Djäkn''']. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Var 1559''' gift med Mats Knutsson, till Sarvlax (Creutz) i Perno sn i Nyland, som omnämnes 1541-1574. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Uppgiften att''' han levat 1584, visar sig vid granskning av källstället oriktig. Som anvapen finnes Bengtas vapen »ett hängande silverankar mellan två sexuddiga guldstjärnor i blått fält»* avmålat i Mörskoms kyrka i Östra Nyla
2 CONC nd.
2 CONT
2 CONT  *Please see the sister's (Estrid) profile. And her (Djäkn, Lydikasönernas) coat-of-arms. It is not "A silver anchor with two six-spiked yellow stars on blue." <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT  However, the Creutz's coat-of-arms (please, see the spouse) has a cross in it, perhaps silver, which can be interpreted to be an anchor. They used to be like that. Only in 3D. It's on blue, and it has four six-spiked yellow stars
2 CONC . <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT  Chances are, then, that the dame here, and by proxy, her husband (Matts Knutsson (Creutz) have, for some reason, been buried in Mäntsälä (Mörskom) church. Even if it is not that close to Pernaja (Sarvlaks, Pernå) or Porvoo (Kråkö
2 CONC , Borgå). 
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://runeberg.org/frfinl/0253.html '''Benkta Lydiksdotter'''], lefde 1559. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift med''' Matts Knutsson, till Sarvlaks (Creutz, n:o 96) i Pärnå socken. Han fick 1574 rätt att med sin aflidne sons barn besitta Kråkö under frälse.
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Samma som'''   https://www.geni.com/people/Lydik-Diekn-till-Kr%C3%A5k%C3%B6/6000000004160989340
