1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://minerva.riddarhuset.se/att/stuart-2/
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == HANS STUART (otherwise JOHANNES STUART) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hans Stuart, here treated, is reported to be the son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Stewart/6000000092371603821?through=6000000000410558676 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Agneta-Forbes/6000000092370871932?through
2 CONC =6000000000410558676 [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Stuart_nr_86#TAB_2 Adelsvapen-Wiki: Stuart No. 86]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hans_Stuart Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hans Stuart, "''here treated''" is reported to be the son of  Alexander Stewart, 2nd Lord Orchitree, and Jean Forbes.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Stewart,_2nd_Lord_Ochiltree '''Wikipedia''' (Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Orchitree - kids.  ]) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Working links 2026:
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://www.nashultshembygd.se/nashultsbor/alexander-stuart-de-skotska-kungarnas-frande-i-odmundetorp/ Alexander Stuart, de skotska kungarnas frände i Ödmundetorp]
2 CONT * [https://wallbring.se/Bouppteckningar/david%20stuarts%20utsagor Wallbring]
2 CONT * [https://familjenbostrom.se/genealogi/norrbotten/Artiklar-Ulf/henning.html Boström]
2 CONT * [https://www.stewartsociety.org/history-of-the-stewarts.cfm?section=famous-stewarts&subcatid=18&histid=3566 Stewart Society] (even St. Andrews is right sometimes)
2 CONT * [https://kids.kiddle.co/Andrew_Stewart,_2nd_Lord_Ochiltree Facts]
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Parentage of Hans Stewart ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Mest troliga föräldrar var https://www.geni.com/people/Andrew-Stewart-2nd-Lord-Ochiltree/6000000004391877789 i hans utomäktenskapliga relation med https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Forbes-Countess-of-Atholl/6000000008630790120 enl
2 CONC igt http://ulfhlars.se/Genealogi/Hans_Stuart/Hans%20Stuart%202008-11-02.. De anor som anges på geni anses inte ha existerat.
2 CONT
2 CONT Most likely parents were Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Ochiltree in his extramarital affair with Lady Janet Forbes, Countess of Atholl according to
2 CONT [http://ulfhlars.se/Genealogi/Hans_Stuart/Hans%20Stuart%202008-11-02 dead link images of which can be found] as well as references to the analysis which
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Stuart_nr_86#TAB_2 Adelsvapen-Wiki: Stuart No. 86]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Wiki Translation==
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Stuart was born in Scotland. He was the son of Johannes Stuart and Agneta Forbes. Stuart moved to Sweden and became a cavalry captain in King Eric XIV’s army. He then served Duke Charles of Södermanland and, in 1604, became a
2 CONC  chamberlain in his service. Stuart later became colonel of a regiment of Scottish mercenaries. He subsequently became quartermaster-general and general commissary of war, as well as general mustermaster over all foreign troops in
2 CONC  Sweden in 1609. Stuart died in 1618 and was buried next to his wife in Vadsbro Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1600 to 1608, he served as district judge in Lysings District.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Property===
2 CONT
2 CONT Stuart owned the estates of Hedenlunda in Vadsbro Parish, Ekskogen in Vadsbro Parish, Rockelsta in Helgesta Parish, and Lida Estate in Kvillinge Parish. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT
2 CONT Stuart was married to Brita Eriksdotter (Soop) (died 1622), daughter of the bailiff Erik Pedersson Soop and Anna Carlsdotter Månesköld af Seglinge in Örebro. Together they had the children Chamberlain Anders Stuart the Younger (15
2 CONC 89–1679), Ingeborg Stuart, Anna Stuart (died 1670), who was married to Lieutenant Colonel [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_Adolph_Stuart Johan Adolf Stuart], Märta Stuart, who was married to Lieutenant Colonel Anton Ydron, and
2 CONC  Chamberlain [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Stuart David Stuart] (1595–1657). [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anders_Stuart_den_%C3%A4ldre Anders Stuart Sr.] was his brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Swedish==
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Stuart, den förste av den svenska grenen av släkten Stuart, inkom till Sverige i september 1565. Han får 1585 i ett sköldebrev[2] av Jacob VI av Skottland det vapen som den svenska släkten Stuart fortfarande bär. Detta vapen 
2 CONC visar att Hans Stuart tillhör den skotska släktgrenen ”Stewart of Avandale/Ochiltree”[3]. I Elgenstiernas ättartavlor[4] anges Hans föräldrar vara riddaren och översten John Stuart samt Agneta Forbes. Denna uppgift kan ledas tillb
2 CONC aka till en uppgift[5] från David Stuart, Hans Stuarts yngre son. David Stuart anger även att hans farföräldrar bott i Edinburgh samt att hans farfars far hette Thomas Stuart. Att Hans Stuart är från Edinburgh anges också i ett ”b
2 CONC ördsintyg”[6] undertecknat 1579 i Edinburgh av sex skotska adelsmän, varav tre är medlemmar av det skotska rådet (”Privy Council”). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===English Translation===
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Stuart, the first of the Swedish branch of the Stuart family, came to Sweden in September 1565. In 1585 he receives in a shield letter [2] from Jacob VI of Scotland the weapon that the Swedish family Stuart still carries. Thi
2 CONC s coat of arms shows that Hans Stuart belongs to the Scottish family branch "Stewart of Avandale / Ochiltree" [3]. In Elgenstierna's pedigrees [4], his parents are stated to be the knight and colonel John Stuart and Agneta Forbes.
2 CONC  This task can be traced back to a task [5] from David Stuart, Hans Stuart's younger son. David Stuart also states that his grandparents lived in Edinburgh and that his grandfather's father's name was Thomas Stuart. Hans Stuart's 
2 CONC of Edinburgh is also stated in a "birth certificate" [6] signed in Edinburgh in 1579 by six Scottish nobles, three of whom are members of the Scottish Privy Council.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Swedish==
2 CONT
2 CONT En släktutredning inlämnades 1762 av huvudmannen Carl Petter Stuart till Riddarhuset[7]. I denna har en ”Anders Stuart, riddare” infogats. Anders har försetts med en hustru ”Brita Douglas”. Släkten anges här felaktigt vara ”till O
2 CONC rkney.  I Elgenstiernas ättartavlor[8] är detta rättats till Ochiltree men i övrigt är 1762 års antavla basen för Stuart tabell 1. De i tabell 1 angivna personerna är tyvärr inte historiska personer och alla försök att identifiera
2 CONC  dem har varit fåfänga.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===English Translation===
2 CONT
2 CONT A genealogy was submitted in 1762 by the principal Carl Petter Stuart to the House of Knights [7]. In this, an "Anders Stuart, knight" has been inserted. Anders has been provided with a wife "Brita Douglas". The family is incorrec
2 CONC tly stated here to be "to Orkney. In Elgenstierna's genealogies [8] this has been corrected to Ochiltree but otherwise the 1762 pedigree is the basis for Stuart table 1. The persons listed in table 1 are unfortunately not historic
2 CONC al persons and all attempts to identify them have been in vain.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Swedish==
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl-Erik Hortling publicerade 1983 en artikel i ”The Stewarts”[9]. Hortling hade sett vapenskölden för familjen Avandale/Ochiltree i ett slott i franska Veziennes. Det vapen som Hortling beskriver kan kallas det traditionella Ava
2 CONC ndale/Ochiltree vapnet (se nedan). Hortlings försök att ge Hans Stuart franska anor övertygar inte. Hortling kände inte till David Stuarts utsagor när han skrev artikeln. Davids utsagor samt de två pergamentsbreven, se nedan, tyde
2 CONC r på att Hans Stuart har en genuin skotsk bakgrund. Däremot så tror jag inte att David visste vilka som var hans faders föräldrar, vilket Hortling lär fått höra från den dåvarande riddarhusgenealogen Pontus Möller. Den senare har 
2 CONC gjort en avskrift av dokumentet som finns i Riddarhusets arkiv.
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl-Erik Hortling published an article in 1983 in "The Stewarts" [9]. Hortling had seen the coat of arms of the Avandale / Ochiltree family in a castle in Veziennes, France. The weapon that Hortling describes can be called the tr
2 CONC aditional Avandale / Ochiltree weapon (see below). Hortling's attempt to give Hans Stuart French ancestry is not convincing. Hortling did not know David Stuart's statements when he wrote the article. David's statements and the two
2 CONC  parchment letters, see below, indicate that Hans Stuart has a genuine Scottish background. On the other hand, I do not think that David knew who his father's parents were, which Hortling is said to have heard from the then knight
2 CONC 's house genealogist Pontus Möller. The latter has made a copy of the document which is in Riddarhuset's archive.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Interlude:
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Heraldic Analysis of the Stuart Coat of Arms==
2 CONT
2 CONT The image is a quarterly shield, which is a traditional way of combining several lineages or titles into a single coat of arms. It accurately reflects the complex history of the House of Stewart (Stuart).
2 CONT ​
2 CONT ===Breakdown of the Quarters===
2 CONT ​
2 CONT '''First Quarter''' (Top Left): This features the Royal Arms of Scotland. It displays a red lion rampant (standing on its hind legs) within a red "double tressure flory-counter-flory" (the decorative border with fleurs-de-lis) on 
2 CONC a gold field. This represents the family’s long reign as Kings and Queens of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ​'''Second Quarter''' (Top Right): This shows a gold field with a blue and silver checkered band (fess chequy). This is the original and most famous emblem of the High Stewards of Scotland. The checkered pattern is said to represe
2 CONC nt the cloth used by the early Stewards for counting money in their role as royal treasurers.
2 CONT ​
2 CONT '''Third Quarter''' (Bottom Left): This depicts a red diagonal cross (saltire) between four red roses on a silver field. This is the coat of arms of the House of Lennox. The Stuart of Lennox branch was a major cadet branch; notabl
2 CONC y, Lord Darnley (Mary Queen of Scots' husband) belonged to this line.
2 CONT ​
2 CONT '''Fourth Quarter''' (Bottom Right): This displays a gold lion rampant on a red field. This is the traditional arms of the Earldom of Fife, an ancient Scottish title that became linked to the Stewarts through marriage and inherita
2 CONC nce.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===​Conclusion===
2 CONT
2 CONT ​The image is a very faithful representation of a high-ranking member of the Stuart dynasty. Rather than being a simple family crest, it is a compositional shield that tells the story of the family's rise to royalty and their stra
2 CONC tegic alliances with other powerful Scottish noble houses.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Heraldic Analysis: The 1585 Patent of Nobility for Hans Stuart (Sköldebrev)==
2 CONT
2 CONT ​This document, issued by King James VI of Scotland, served as the primary evidence of nobility required for the family’s naturalization into the Swedish House of Nobility (Adelsätten Stuart, No. 86). The coat of arms is a sophist
2 CONC icated display of high-ranking Scottish lineage, structured to emphasize the family's connections to the Stewart and Lennox dynasties.
2 CONT
2 CONT ​1. The Stewart and Lennox Quarters (The Paternal Lineage) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ​The main shield is divided into four quarters, each representing a specific branch of the family tree in Scotland:
2 CONT
2 CONT ​First and Fourth Quarters (The Royal Lion): Features a red lion rampant within a flory-counter-flory border on a gold field. This is the Royal Arms of Scotland, used here to signify the family's descent from the royal Stewart lin
2 CONC e. ​Second Quarter (The Stewart Fess): Displays the fess chequy (a blue and silver checkered band), which is the fundamental heraldic mark of the House of Stewart. Above the band is a red lion, a specific identifier for the Stewar
2 CONC t of Lennox branch. ​Third Quarter (The Lennox Saltire): Shows a black saltire (diagonal cross) accompanied by four red roses. This is the historic coat of arms of the Earls of Lennox, further anchoring Hans Stuart's pedigree in t
2 CONC he Scottish peerage. ​2. The Forbes Exception (The Heart Shield) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ​As a notable exception to the purely paternal Stewart iconography, the center of the shield features a heart shield (escutcheon of pretence).
2 CONT
2 CONT ​The Motif: It depicts a silver galley (ship) on a blue field. ​The Forbes Connection: This central position is reserved for the Forbes lineage. While the traditional Scottish Forbes arms consist of three bears' heads, this Swedis
2 CONC h version utilizes the galley—a variation that became the standardized representation for this branch in Sweden. Its placement in the center signifies that the Forbes heritage is a vital, integrated component of this specific fami
2 CONC ly’s identity. ​3. External Ornaments and Authority ​The Crest: Above the barred knight’s helmet sit two stars (or spur-rowels), which are traditional heraldic ornaments for this branch. ​Royal Validation: The prominent text "JACO
2 CONC BUS DEI GRATIA REX SCOTORUM" (James, by the Grace of God, King of Scots) validates the authenticity of these arms. This royal recognition was the "gold standard" for gaining acceptance into the Swedish aristocracy, proving that th
2 CONC e bearer was of "ancient and knightly" origin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT - If there's a referefence to the family Forbes - the reason of rule posits that there IS a reason.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Swedish==
2 CONT
2 CONT Leo Hilden har i en artikel i ”The Scottish Genealogist” [10] försökt påvisa vem Hans Stuarts far ”överste John Stewart var och varför han inte finns dokumenterad i Skotska dokument.  Den tyska källan ha anger bygger troligen på d
2 CONC et svenska som är baserat på David Stewart som dock inte anger att Hans Stuarts fader John Stewart kom med sin son till Sverige. Den ende som man kanske skulle kunna kalla ”John Stewart till Ochiltree” var Henry Stewarts, Lord Met
2 CONC hvens, son John ”the master of Methven” som dog i slaget vid Pinkie i september 1547.  Den John Stewart som enligt David Stuart skulle ha följt med drottning Maria av Skottland till Frankrike är tyvärr inte en historisk person och
2 CONC  Leo Hildens försök att identifiera honom övertygar inte.
2 CONT
2 CONT In an article in "The Scottish Genealogist" [10], Leo Hilden has tried to prove who Hans Stuart's father "Colonel John Stewart was and why he is not documented in Scottish documents. The German source ha states is probably based o
2 CONC n the Swedish which is based on David Stewart who does not state that Hans Stuart's father John Stewart came with his son to Sweden. The only one who could perhaps be called "John Stewart to Ochiltree" was Henry Stewarts, Lord Met
2 CONC hvens, son John "the master of Methven" who died in the battle of Pinkie in September 1547. The John Stewart who according to David Stuart would have followed Queen Mary of Scotland to France is unfortunately not a historical figu
2 CONC re and Leo Hilden's attempts to identify him are not convincing.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Swedish==
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Joëlson var vänlig och gav mig del av hans material om Hans Stuart, bl.a. av hans broder år 1956 avtecknade gravhällar och begravningsvapen i Vadsbro kyrka, brev till riddarhusgenealogen Pontus Möller, brev från Hortling till
2 CONC  Jacob Stuart, Harald Stuarts översättningar av de skotska breven, David Stuarts utsagor om sin faders släkts från Peringskiölds genealogier och Carl-Erik Hortlings artikel från 1983 i ”The Stewart Magazine”.  Han hade dock ingen 
2 CONC färdig teori om vilka Hans Stuarts föräldrar egentligen var. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Joëlson was kind and gave me some of his material about Hans Stuart, i.a. of his brother in 1956 signed gravestones and funeral coats of arms in Vadsbro church, letters to the knight's house genealogist Pontus Möller, letters
2 CONC  from Hortling to Jacob Stuart, Harald Stuart's translations of the Scottish letters, David Stuart's statements about his father's family from Peringskiöld's genealogies and Carl-Erik Hortling's article from 1983 in "The Stewart M
2 CONC agazine". However, he had no complete theory about who Hans Stuart's parents really were. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Swedish==
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Stuart, äldste sonen till Hans Stuart, som dör den 9/5 1679, har på sin gravsten åtta skotska vapen som borde representerande faderns, Hans Stuarts skotska släkt samt åtta vapen representerande moderns, Brita Soops svenska 
2 CONC släkt[11]. Samtliga åtta skotska vapen är här, med vissa reservationer, identifierade och har gett ledtrådar till Hans Stuarts liv i Skottland samt vem som möjligen kan ha varit hans moder. De i familjen Stuart som beställde begra
2 CONC  vningsvapnen visste nog inte mer än David Stuart om de skotska anorna som vapnen skulle föreställa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Stuart, the eldest son of Hans Stuart, who died on 9/5 1679, has on his tombstone eight Scottish coats of arms that should represent his father, Hans Stuart's Scottish family and eight coats of arms representing his mother,
2 CONC  Brita Soop's Swedish family [11]. All eight Scottish weapons are here, with some reservations, identified and have provided clues to Hans Stuart's life in Scotland and who may have been his mother. Those in the Stuart family who 
2 CONC ordered the funeral weapons probably knew no more than David Stuart about the Scottish ancestry that the weapons would represent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl-Henrik Stiernspetz har fotograferat av de både breven som förvaras i Riddarhusets arkiv. Har även haft tillgång till dessa foton och år 2002 själv besökt Vadsbro kyrka och då fotograferat gravhällarna och begravningsvapnen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl-Henrik Stiernspetz has photographed both the letters that are stored in Riddarhuset's archives. Has also had access to these photos and in 2002 himself visited Vadsbro church and then photographed the tombstones and funeral c
2 CONC oats.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Swedish==
2 CONT
2 CONT Har läst ett stort antal biografier över personer som levde i Skotland under 1500-talet, skotsk historia med fokus på 1500-talet, skotsk heraldisk litteratur mm, se listan över källor, Besökte Edinburgh och nationalbiblioteken men
2 CONC  hann även besöka en skotsk genealogisk förening som jag då var medlem av. Vidare gjorde jag ett besök på den skotska heraldiska myndigheten ”Lord Lyons Office” och kunde där studera en kopia av ett heraldiskt manuskript, kallat ”
2 CONC the Seaton Armorial” som innehåller den variant av Lord Ochiltrees vapen som Hans Stuarts vapen är baserad på. Ett besök på det skotska riksarkivet räckt för att ta reda att det inte fanns några testamenten bevarade från undersökt
2 CONC a personerna med ett möjligt undantag, Lord Ochiltrees andra hustru har efterlämnat ett testamente, som jag inte studerade. Källförteckningen innehåller dels dokument som jag studerade i Edinburgh dels dokument som jag införskaffa
2 CONC t. Intresset för historia och genealogi är stort i Skottland. Många 1500-tals dokument finns utgivna och min studie är på intet sätt komplett. Men möjligheten att finna ett dokument som klargör vilka Hans Stuarts föräldrar var bed
2 CONC ömer jag som mycket liten. Har i stället försökt samla på indicier. Dessa pekar enligt min mening ut föräldrarna, men man kan ju aldrig vara säker till 100 %.
2 CONT
2 CONT Have read a large number of biographies of people who lived in Scotland during the 16th century, Scottish history with a focus on the 16th century, Scottish heraldic literature etc., see the list of sources, Visited Edinburgh and 
2 CONC the National Libraries but also had time to visit a Scottish genealogical association like me then was a member of. I also visited the Scottish heraldic authority "Lord Lyons Office" and was able to study a copy of a heraldic manu
2 CONC script, called "the Seaton Armorial", which contains the variant of Lord Ochiltree's weapon on which Hans Stuart's weapon is based. A visit to the Scottish National Archives was enough to find out that there were no wills preserve
2 CONC d from the persons examined with a possible exception; Lord Ochiltree's second wife has left a will, which I did not study. The list of sources contains both documents that I studied in Edinburgh and documents that I acquired. The
2 CONC  interest in history and genealogy is great in Scotland. Many 16th century documents have been published and my study is by no means complete. But the opportunity to find a document that clarifies who Hans Stuart's parents were, I
2 CONC  consider very small. Have instead tried to gather clues. In my opinion, these point out the parents, but you can never be 100% sure.
2 CONT
